    {
      "id": "validation",
      "title": "Leave-one-out validation",
      "blurb": "Each observed node is held out in turn and re-imputed from the rest of the graph. Kendall \u03c4-b measures whether held-out predictions recover the ORDER of observed effects; a 95% CI excluding 0 is a significant (positive or negative) result."
    }
